      "title": "Suspect arrested over fire at Hitler’s ‘Eagle’s Nest’ retreat in Bavaria",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/blaze-engulfs-hitlers-eagles-nest-mountain-retreat-in-bavaria",
      "description": "<p>About 200 firefighters deployed to tackle blaze at former Nazi mountain retreat in remote part of southern Germany</p><p>Police have arrested a 33-year-old German citizen after a fire ripped through Adolf Hitler’s former mountain retreat in Bavaria, leaving the historic Nazi meeting place – known as the Eagle’s Nest – largely destroyed.</p><p>About 200 firefighters were deployed on Friday night to tackle the blaze at the Nazi dictator’s remote, purpose-built Kehlsteinhaus residence, a protected building on the peak of Obersalzberg in southern Germany.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/blaze-engulfs-hitlers-eagles-nest-mountain-retreat-in-bavaria\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
